      "metric_value": "14.59390294 kg",
      "metric_unit": "",
      "notes": "The slug, a unit associated with imperial and US customary systems, is a mass that accelerates by 1 ft/s 2 when a force of one pound (lbf) is exerted on it. F = ma ( Newton's second law ) 1 lbf = 1 slug × 1 ft/s 2 (as defined above) 1 lbf = 1 lb × g /gc (by definition of the pound force ) g ≈ 32.174 048 56 ft/s 2 gc ≈ 32.174 048 56 lbm⋅ft/lbf⋅s 2 1 slug ≈ 32.174 048 56 pounds"
